Peter,

I want to take a moment to share what&rsquo;s been happening on the campaign trail. I&rsquo;ve been holding back-to-back town halls and events, traveling across our district, and I&rsquo;ve racked up an incredible 45,000 miles on the campaign car.

https://click.email.judgejoeforcongress.com/?qs=9b2dfa623cb9a076716b1d0d6bf41e2d8b6a7582cb176cfa42b130691e2c74982fa92604a156a17363e424dc23d910f54be54bb6971dd8d9

Why? Because I believe in meeting with you, listening to your concerns, and sharing my vision for a brighter future for IL-17.

I stepped down from the bench to run for Congress because I know our community deserves better than the failed liberal policies he&rsquo;s currently giving us in Washington. We don&rsquo;t need to keep another rubber stamp for the left in DC. We need a leader who will put the needs of our community first&mdash;not the desires of more out-of-touch politicians.

I&rsquo;m committed to earning every single vote, fighting for the issues that matter most to you.

But I need to be honest&mdash;time is running out. Resources are dwindling, and the Democrats are pouring money into this race. My liberal opponent, Eric Sorensen, is launching attacks against me.

But let me be clear: I won&rsquo;t back down. I&rsquo;m in this fight for you, and I&rsquo;ll continue to stand strong.

